  ⚠ react(no-deriving-state-in-effects): Values derived from props and state should be calculated during render, not in an effect
    ╭─[no_deriving_state_in_effects.tsx:8:5]
  7 │   useEffect(() => {
  8 │     setFullName(firstName + ' ' + lastName);
    ·     ─────┬─────
    ·          ╰── This state update stores a value that can be calculated during render
  9 │   }, [firstName, lastName]);
    ·       ────┬────  ────────
    ·           ╰── These reactive values contribute to the derived state
 10 │   return <div>{fullName}</div>;
    ╰────
  help: This effect derives state from the reactive values `firstName`, `lastName`, causing an extra render and potentially showing a stale value. Calculate the derived value during render, then remove the redundant state and effect.
  note: React Compiler skipped optimizing this component or hook. Additional guidance: https://react.dev/reference/eslint-plugin-react-hooks/lints/set-state-in-effect
